@markstory It's a general problem that will occour whenever a non-to string convertable value is the select list of a containment.

**https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/3.3.2/src/ORM/Association/SelectableAssociationTrait.php#L137**

The select list is being passed into `array_diff()` as is, where the object will be tried to be converted to a string, which results into an error, and combined with a PHP bug/quirk present in PHP < 7.0, the diff will not find the foreign key in the select list in case it is placed directly after the field that has the function expression, causing the missing select exception to be thrown.

You probably won't be able to see the latter problem when testing the core, not without additional measures, as there is no error handler registered that would trigger the PHP quirk (cakes default handler does trigger it).

``` php
public function testExpressionInContainableSelectListWithPhpErrorHandlerArrayQuirkPresent()
{
    $oldHandler = set_error_handler(function ($errno, $errstr, $errfile, $errline) {
        if ($errno === E_RECOVERABLE_ERROR) {
            $foo = [];
            asort($foo);
            echo $errstr . PHP_EOL;
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    });

    try {
        $Articles = TableRegistry::get('Articles');
        $Articles->hasMany('Comments');

        $query = $Articles
            ->find()
            ->contain([
                'Comments' => function (Query $q) {
                    return $q
                        ->select([
                            'computed' => $q->func()->count('id'),
                            'article_id'
                        ]);
                }
            ]);
        $query->all();
    } finally {
        set_error_handler($oldHandler);
    }
}
```

